866 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2624 0 R
/E (In Von Neumann architecture, data and instructions are stored on the same memory. CPU only can read an instruction or a data at the same time. In Harvard architecture, data and instructions are stored separately, and each one has its own bus. CPU can read both at the same time \(an instruction and a data\). )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
867 0 obj
<<
